Package: rflpSNP
Title: In Silico Design and Simulation of PCR-RFLP and ARMS-PCR Assays for SNP Genotyping
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Miguel", "Esparza", , "esparzamiguel057@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Miguel Esparza [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Miguel Esparza <esparzamiguel057@gmail.com>
Description: Tools to design PCR-RFLP and tetra-primer ARMS-PCR assays from a
    reference sequence in FASTA format and a dbSNP flanking sequence. It
    evaluates physicochemical properties (Tm, %GC, dimers and hairpins),
    simulates PCR products on reference and alternate alleles, and predicts
    agarose-gel band patterns for the three possible genotypes. Intended as a
    teaching and reproducibility tool for in-silico SNP genotyping assay design.
